DG.put("chaubees-avtaar-2/6",{"n":6,"title":null,"title_roman":null,"page":772,"blocks":[{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਪਾਧਰੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਪਾਧਰੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Paadhree chhand","meaning_en":"Padhari metre.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[511],"number_text":"੫੧੧।","page":772,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਪੂਰਬ ਪਟਨ ਉਪਟਿ। ਖੰਡੇ ਅਖੰਡ ਕਟੇ ਅਕਟ।","roman":"Ih bhaati poorab patan upti | khande akhand kate akat |","meaning_en":"In this way he uprooted the cities of the east; he broke the unbroken and cut down the uncut;","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਟਨ ਉਪਟਿ: 'uprooted the cities (pattan)'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਫਟੇ ਅਫਟ ਖੰਡੇ ਅਖੰਡ। ਬਜੇ ਨਿਸਾਨ ਮਚਿਓ ਘਮੰਡ। ੫੧੧।","roman":"Phate aphat khande akhand | baje nisaan machio ghamand | 511 |","meaning_en":"he split the unsplit and shattered the unshattered; the drums sounded and pride ran high.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[512],"number_text":"੫੧੨।","page":772,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਰੇ ਸੁ ਜੰਗ ਜੋਧਾ ਜੁਝਾਰ। ਜੋ ਤਜੇ ਬਾਣ ਗਜਤ ਲੁਝਾਰ।","roman":"Jore su jang jodhaa jujhaar | jo taje baan gajat lujhaar |","meaning_en":"The fighting warriors joined battle; the combatants roared as they loosed their arrows.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਜੰਤ ਭੀਰ ਭਹਰੰਤ ਭਾਇ। ਭਭਕੰਤ ਘਾਇ ਡਿੱਗੇ ਅਘਾਇ। ੫੧੨।","roman":"Bhaajant bheer bhahrant bhaai | bhabhkant ghaai digge aghaai | 512 |","meaning_en":"The cowards fled, shaking with fear; wounds gushed, and (the warriors) fell, sated.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਘਾਇ: 'sated' (with fighting); uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[513],"number_text":"੫੧੩।","page":772,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਜੰਤ ਸਾਜ ਬਾਜਤ ਤੁਫੰਗ। ਨਾਚੰਤ ਭੂਤ ਭੈਧਰ ਸੁਰੰਗ।","roman":"Saajant saaj baajat tuphang | naachant bhoot bhaidhar surang |","meaning_en":"Equipped with their gear, the muskets fire; ghosts in fearsome, fine colours dance;","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭੈਧਰ ਸੁਰੰਗ: 'fearsome, brightly coloured'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਬਕੰਤ ਬਿਤਾਲ ਕਹਕੰਤ ਕਾਲ। ਡਮਕੰਤ ਡਉਰ ਮੁਕਤੰਤ ਜ੍ਵਾਲ। ੫੧੩।","roman":"Babkant bitaal kahkant kaal | damkant daur muktant jvaal | 513 |","meaning_en":"the Baitals howl, Kal (Kali) laughs, the damru drum rattles and flames shoot out.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[514],"number_text":"੫੧੪।","page":772,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਜੰਤ ਭੀਰ ਤਜਿ ਬੀਰ ਖੇਤ। ਨਾਚੰਤ ਭੂਤ ਬੇਤਾਲ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ।","roman":"Bhaajant bheer taji beer khet | naachant bhoot betaal pret |","meaning_en":"The cowards flee, leaving the field of heroes; ghosts, Baitals and spirits dance.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰੀੜੰਤ ਈਸ ਪੋਅੰਤ ਕਪਾਲ। ਨਿਰਖਤ ਬੀਰ ਛਕਿ ਬਰਤ ਬਾਲ। ੫੧੪।","roman":"Kreerant ees poant kapaal | nirkhat beer chhaki barat baal | 514 |","meaning_en":"Shiva sports, stringing skulls; the maidens (of heaven) gaze at the heroes and, delighted, wed them.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[515],"number_text":"੫੧੫।","page":772,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਵੰਤ ਬੀਰ ਬਾਹੰਤ ਘਾਵ। ਨਾਚੰਤ ਭੂਤ ਗਾਵੰਤ ਚਾਵ।","roman":"Dhaavant beer baahant ghaav | naachant bhoot gaavant chaav |","meaning_en":"The heroes charge and deal wounds; ghosts dance and sing with joy.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਮਕੰਤ ਡਉਰੁ ਨਾਚੰਤ ਈਸ। ਰੀਝੰਤ ਹਿਮਦ੍ਰਿ ਅੰਤ ਸੀਸ। ੫੧੫।","roman":"Damkant dauru naachant ees | reejhant himdri ant sees | 515 |","meaning_en":"The damru rattles and Shiva dances; the one (dwelling) at the end of the Himalaya is pleased in his head.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੀਝੰਤ ਹਿਮਦ੍ਰਿ ਅੰਤ ਸੀਸ: read as 'Shiva, of the Himalaya's peak, rejoices'; very uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[516],"number_text":"੫੧੬।","page":772,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗੰਧ੍ਰਭ ਸਿਧ ਚਾਰਣ ਪ੍ਰਸਿਧ। ਕਥੰਤ ਕਾਬਿ ਸੋਭੰਤ ਸਿਧ।","roman":"Gandhrabh sidh chaaran prasidh | kathant kaabi sobhant sidh |","meaning_en":"Gandharvas, Siddhas and famed Charans recite poems, and the Siddhas look splendid;","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਾਵੰਤ ਬੀਨ ਬੀਨਾ ਬਜੰਤ। ਰੀਝੰਤ ਦੇਵ ਮੁਨਿ ਮਨਿ ਡੁਲੰਤ। ੫੧੬।","roman":"Gaavant been beenaa bajant | reejhant dev muni mani dulant | 516 |","meaning_en":"they sing and play the vina; the gods are pleased, and the minds of the sages waver.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[517],"number_text":"੫੧੭।","page":772,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗੁੰਜਤ ਗਜਿੰਦ੍ਰ ਹੈਵਰ ਅਸੰਖ। ਬੁਲਤ ਸੁਬਾਹ ਮਾਰੂ ਬਜੰਤ।","roman":"Gunjat gajindr haivar asankh | bulat subaah maaroo bajant |","meaning_en":"Mighty elephants and countless fine horses roar; the heroes cry out and the war-music plays.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਬਾਹ: 'heroes (of fine arms)'; ਮਾਰੂ: martial music."},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠੰਤ ਨਾਦ ਪੂਰਤ ਦਿਸਾਣੰ। ਡੁਲਤ ਮਹੇਂਦ੍ਰ ਮਹਿ ਧਰ ਮਹਾਣੰ। ੫੧੭।","roman":"Uthant naad poorat disaanan | dulat mahendr mahi dhar mahaanan | 517 |","meaning_en":"The sound rises and fills the directions; Indra and the great mountains of the earth shake.","page":772,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਹੇਂਦ੍ਰ: Indra, or the Mahendra mountain; ਮਹਿ ਧਰ: 'earth-holders' (mountains). Uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[518],"number_text":"੫੧੮।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖੁਲੰਤ ਖੇਤਿ ਖੂਨੀ ਖਤੰਗ। ਛੁਟੰਤ ਬਾਣ ਜੁਟੇ ਨਿਸੰਗ।","roman":"Khulant kheti khoonee khatang | chhutant baan jute nisang |","meaning_en":"On the field the bloody arrows are drawn; arrows fly, and the fearless ones close in.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖਤੰਗ: 'arrow' (Persian khadang)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਿਦੰਤ ਮਰਮ ਜੁਝਤ ਸੁਬਾਹ। ਘੁਮੰਤ ਗੈਣਿ ਅਛ੍ਰੀ ਉਛਾਹ। ੫੧੮।","roman":"Bhidant maram jujhat subaah | ghumant gaini achhree uchhaah | 518 |","meaning_en":"Vital points are pierced, the heroes fight; the apsaras circle the sky with eagerness.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[519],"number_text":"੫੧੯।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰਖੰਤ ਸੇਲ ਬਰਖੰਤ ਬਾਣ। ਹਰਖੰਤ ਹੂਰ ਪਰਖੰਤ ਜੁਆਣ।","roman":"Sarkhant sel barkhant baan | harkhant hoor parkhant juaan |","meaning_en":"Lances flash, arrows rain down; the houris rejoice, testing the young men.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਰਖੰਤ: 'move/flash'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਜੰਤ ਢੋਲ ਡਉਰੂ ਕਰਾਲ। ਨਾਚੰਤ ਭੂਤ ਭੈਰੋ ਕਪਾਲਿ। ੫੧੯।","roman":"Baajant dhol dauroo karaal | naachant bhoot bhairo kapaali | 519 |","meaning_en":"Drums and fearsome damrus sound; ghosts dance, and Bhairav and the skull-bearer.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[520],"number_text":"੫੨੦।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰੜੰਤ ਹਥ ਖਰੜੰਤ ਖੋਲ। ਟਿਰੜੰਤ ਟੀਕ ਝਿਰੜੰਤ ਝੋਲ।","roman":"Harrant hath kharrant khol | tirrant teek jhirrant jhol |","meaning_en":"Hands clatter, sheaths rattle, (blows) thud and pouches(?) rustle;","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Largely sound-words (ਹਰੜੰਤ, ਖਰੜੰਤ, ਟਿਰੜੰਤ, ਝਿਰੜੰਤ); ਟੀਕ/ਝੋਲ uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਰੜੰਤ ਦੀਹ ਦਾਨੋ ਦੁਰੰਤ। ਹਰੜੰਤ ਹਾਸ ਹਸਤ ਮਹੰਤ। ੫੨੦।","roman":"Darrant deeh daano durant | harrant haas hasat mahant | 520 |","meaning_en":"the huge, evil demons are crushed; the great ones laugh a roaring laugh.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਰੜੰਤ: 'crush'; ਮਹੰਤ: 'great ones'. Sound-words in places."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਉਤਭੁਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਉਤਭੁਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Utbhuj chhand","meaning_en":"Utbhuj metre.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[521],"number_text":"੫੨੧।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਹਾਸੰ ਕਪਾਲੰ। ਸੁ ਬਾਸੰ ਛਤਾਲੰ।","roman":"Hahaasan kapaalan | su baasan chhataalan |","meaning_en":"The skull-bearer laughs aloud; (the field) is fragrant, full of dancing(?);","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁ ਬਾਸੰ ਛਤਾਲੰ: uncertain; perhaps 'well adorned, with clapping rhythm'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਭਾਸੰ ਜ੍ਵਾਲੰ। ਅਨਾਸੰ ਕਰਾਲੰ। ੫੨੧।","roman":"Prabhaasan jvaalan | anaasan karaalan | 521 |","meaning_en":"flames shine forth, fearsome and undying.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਨਾਸੰ: 'imperishable'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[522],"number_text":"੫੨੨।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਰੂਪ ਧਾਰੇ। ਦੁਰੰ ਦੁਖ ਤਾਰੇ।","roman":"Mahaa roop dhaare | duran dukh taare |","meaning_en":"He took a mighty form, and carried (people) across hard sorrows;","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰੰਨੀ ਉਧਾਰੇ। ਅਘੀ ਪਾਪ ਵਾਰੇ। ੫੨੨।","roman":"Sarannee udhaare | aghee paap vaare | 522 |","meaning_en":"he saved those who came to his refuge, and took away the sins of the sinful.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[523],"number_text":"੫੨੩।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦਿਪੈ ਜੋਤਿ ਜ੍ਵਾਲਾ। ਕਿਧੌ ਜ੍ਵਾਲ ਮਾਲਾ।","roman":"Dipai joti jvaalaa | kidhau jvaal maalaa |","meaning_en":"His light blazes like a flame, or like a garland of flames,","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨੋ ਜ੍ਵਾਲ ਬਾਲਾ। ਸਰੂਪੰ ਕਰਾਲਾ। ੫੨੩।","roman":"Mano jvaal baalaa | saroopan karaalaa | 523 |","meaning_en":"as if a young flame; his form is awesome.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[524],"number_text":"੫੨੪।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰੇ ਖਗ ਪਾਣੰ। ਤਿਹੂੰ ਲੋਗ ਮਾਣੰ।","roman":"Dhare khag paanan | tihoon log maanan |","meaning_en":"He bears the sword in his hand; he is honoured in the three worlds.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਯੰ ਦੀਹ ਦਾਨੰ। ਭਰੇ ਸਉਜ ਮਾਨੰ। ੫੨੪।","roman":"Dayan deeh daanan | bhare sauj maanan | 524 |","meaning_en":"He gives great gifts, and is full of all honour.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਉਜ ਮਾਨੰ: 'all honour/regard'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅਜੰਨ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਅਜੰਨ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Ajann chhand","meaning_en":"Ajann metre.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[525],"number_text":"੫੨੫।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਜੀਤੇ ਜੀਤ ਜੀਤ ਕੈ। ਅਭੀਰੀ ਭਾਜੇ ਭੀਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ।","roman":"Ajeete jeet jeet kai | abheeree bhaaje bheer hvai |","meaning_en":"Conquering again and again the unconquered, the fearless ones were made to flee in fear;","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਧਾਰੇ ਚੀਨ ਰਾਜ ਪੈ। ਸਥੋਈ ਸਰਬ ਸਾਥ ਕੈ। ੫੨੫।","roman":"Sidhaare cheen raaj pai | sathoee sarab saath kai | 525 |","meaning_en":"he set out against the king of China, taking all his companions with him.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[526],"number_text":"੫੨੬।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਮੰਕੇ ਰਾਜਧਾਰੀ ਕੈ। ਰਜੀਲੇ ਰੋਹਵਾਰੀ ਕੈ।","roman":"Tamanke raajdhaaree kai | rajeele rohvaaree kai |","meaning_en":"(Warriors) of the royal houses flare up, the proud men of Roh;","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਮੰਕੇ: 'flare/blaze up'; ਰੋਹਵਾਰੀ: of Roh. Uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਟੀਲੇ ਕਾਮ ਰੂਪਾ ਕੈ। ਕੰਬੋਜੇ ਕਾਸਕਾਰੀ ਕੈ। ੫੨੬।","roman":"Kaateele kaam roopaa kai | kanboje kaaskaaree kai | 526 |","meaning_en":"the sharp men of Kamrup, the Kambojas and the men of Kashkar.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਟੀਲੇ: 'sharp/cutting'; ਕਾਸਕਾਰੀ: Kashkar/Kashgar. Uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[527],"number_text":"੫੨੭।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਢਮੰਕੇ ਢੋਲ ਢਾਲੋ ਕੈ। ਡਮੰਕੇ ਡੰਕ ਵਾਰੋ ਕੈ।","roman":"Dhamanke dhol dhaalo kai | damanke dank vaaro kai |","meaning_en":"The drums of the shield-bearers boom; the drums of the drum-bearers rattle;","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਮੰਕੇ ਨੇਜ ਬਾਜਾ ਦੇ। ਤਮੰਕੇ ਤੀਰ ਤਾਜਾ ਦੇ। ੫੨੭।","roman":"Ghamanke nej baajaa de | tamanke teer taajaa de | 527 |","meaning_en":"lances flash with the music; fresh arrows glint.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤੀਰ ਤਾਜਾ: 'fresh arrows' or 'arrows of Taj (Arabs)'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਪਾਧਰੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਪਾਧਰੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Paadhree chhand","meaning_en":"Padhari metre.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[528],"number_text":"੫੨੮।","page":773,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੀਤੇ ਅਜੀਤ ਮੰਡੇ ਅਮੰਡ। ਤੋਰੇ ਅਤੋਰ ਖੰਡੇ ਅਖੰਡ।","roman":"Jeete ajeet mande amand | tore ator khande akhand |","meaning_en":"He conquered the unconquered, engaged those never engaged, broke the unbroken and shattered the unshattered;","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੰਨੇ ਅਭੰਨ ਭਜੇ ਅਭਜਿ। ਖਾਨੇ ਖਵਾਸ ਮਾਵਾਸ ਤਜਿ। ੫੨੮।","roman":"Bhanne abhann bhaje abhji | khaane khavaas maavaas taji | 528 |","meaning_en":"he smashed the unsmashed, and those who never fled fled; khans and nobles left their strongholds.","page":773,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖਵਾਸ: 'courtiers/nobles'; ਮਾਵਾਸ: 'stronghold'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[529],"number_text":"੫੨੯।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਕੜੇ ਸੂਰ ਭੰਭਰੇ ਭੀਰ ਨਿਰਖੰਤ ਜੋਧ ਰੀਝੰਤ ਹੂਰ।","roman":"Sankre soor bhanbhre bheer nirkhant jodh reejhant hoor |","meaning_en":"The heroes pressed close, the cowards trembled; the houris watch the warriors and are pleased.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੰਕੜੇ: 'pressed together' or 'shrank'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਾਰੰਤ ਸੀਸ ਕੇਸਰ ਕਟੋਰਿ। ਮ੍ਰਿਗ ਮਦ ਗੁਲਾਬ ਕਰਪੂਰ ਘੋਰਿ। ੫੨੯।","roman":"Daarant sees kesar katori | mrig mad gulaab karpoor ghori | 529 |","meaning_en":"They pour on (the heroes') heads bowls of saffron, mixed with musk, rose and camphor.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[530],"number_text":"੫੩੦।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਜੀਤ ਤੀਨੰ ਦਿਸਾਣ। ਬਜਿਓ ਸੁਕੋਪ ਉਤਰ ਨਿਸਾਣ।","roman":"Ih bhaati jeet teenan disaan | bajio sukop utar nisaan |","meaning_en":"In this way he conquered three directions; in wrath the drums sounded for the north.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲੇ ਸੁ ਚੀਨ ਮਾਚੀਨ ਦੇਸਿ। ਸਾਮੰਤ ਸੁਧ ਰਾਵਲੀ ਭੇਖ। ੫੩੦।","roman":"Chale su cheen maacheen desi | saamant sudh raavlee bhekh | 530 |","meaning_en":"They set out for the lands of China and Machin; the nobles (were) in pure Rawal garb.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਾਵਲੀ ਭੇਖ: 'the dress of Rawals (yogis)' or 'royal dress'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[531],"number_text":"੫੩੧।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਜੇ ਬਜੰਤ੍ਰ ਗਜੇ ਸੁਬਾਹ। ਸਾਵੰਤ ਦੇਖਿ ਅਛ੍ਰੀ ਉਛਾਹ।","roman":"Baje bajantr gaje subaah | saavant dekhi achhree uchhaah |","meaning_en":"Instruments play, the heroes roar; seeing the warriors, the apsaras are eager.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੀਝੰਤ ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਸਰਬ। ਗਾਵੰਤ ਗੀਤ ਤਜ ਦੀਨ ਗਰਬ। ੫੩੧।","roman":"Reejhant dev adev sarab | gaavant geet taj deen garab | 531 |","meaning_en":"All the gods and demons are pleased; they sing songs and have set aside their pride.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[532],"number_text":"੫੩੨।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਜਿਓ ਸੁ ਸੈਣ ਸੁਣਿ ਚੀਨ ਰਾਜ। ਬਜੇ ਬਜੰਤ੍ਰ ਸਰਬੰ ਸਮਾਜ।","roman":"Sajio su sain suni cheen raaj | baje bajantr sarban samaaj |","meaning_en":"Hearing this, the king of China made his army ready; instruments sounded throughout the whole host.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲੇ ਅਚਲ ਸਾਵੰਤ ਜੁਧ। ਬਰਖੰਤ ਬਾਣ ਭਰ ਲੋਹ ਕ੍ਰੁਧ। ੫੩੨।","roman":"Chale achal saavant judh | barkhant baan bhar loh krudh | 532 |","meaning_en":"Unshakeable warriors went to war, raining arrows, full of fury and steel.","page":774,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[533],"number_text":"੫੩੩।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖੁਲੇ ਖਤੰਗ ਖੂਨੀ ਖਤ੍ਰਿਹਾਣ। ਉਝਰੇ ਜੁਧ ਜੋਧਾ ਮਹਾਣ।","roman":"Khule khatang khoonee khatrihaan | ujhre judh jodhaa mahaan |","meaning_en":"Bloody arrows that slay Kshatriyas were loosed; great warriors rushed into the fight.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖਤ੍ਰਿਹਾਣ: 'slaying Kshatriyas/warriors'; ਉਝਰੇ: 'rushed/sprang'. Uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਧੁਕੰਤ ਢੋਲ ਘੁੰਮੰਤ ਘਾਇ। ਚਿਕੰਤ ਚਾਵਡੀ ਮਾਸੁ ਚਾਇ। ੫੩੩।","roman":"Dhukant dhol ghunmant ghaai | chikant chaavdee maasu chaai | 533 |","meaning_en":"Drums throb, the wounded reel; the chamundas(?) shriek, eager for flesh.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਾਵਡੀ: read as 'Chamunda/witches' or 'kites'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[534],"number_text":"੫੩੪।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਸੰਤ ਹਾਸ ਕਾਲੀ ਕਰਾਲ। ਭਭਕੰਤ ਭੂਤ ਭੈਰੋ ਬਿਸਾਲ।","roman":"Hasant haas kaalee karaal | bhabhkant bhoot bhairo bisaal |","meaning_en":"Fearsome Kali laughs a loud laugh; ghosts and great Bhairav bellow.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਾਗੰਤ ਬਾਣ ਭਾਖੰਤ ਮਾਸ। ਭਾਜੰਤ ਭੀਰ ਹੁਇ ਹੁਇ ਉਦਾਸ। ੫੩੪।","roman":"Laagant baan bhaakhant maas | bhaajant bheer hui hui udaas | 534 |","meaning_en":"Arrows strike, (the beasts) eat flesh; the cowards flee, utterly downcast.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਾਖੰਤ ਮਾਸ: 'eat flesh' (subject unstated); uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaval metre.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[535],"number_text":"੫੩੫।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚੜਿਓ ਚੀਨ ਰਾਜੰ। ਸਜੇ ਸਰਬ ਸਾਜੰ।","roman":"Chario cheen raajan | saje sarab saajan |","meaning_en":"The king of China rode out, with all his equipment ready.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖੁਲੇ ਖੇਤਿ ਖੂਨੀ। ਚੜੇ ਚੌਪ ਦੂਨੀ। ੫੩੫।","roman":"Khule kheti khoonee | chare chaup doonee | 535 |","meaning_en":"The bloodthirsty (warriors) were let loose on the field, riding out with double eagerness.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[536],"number_text":"੫੩੬।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਟੇ ਜੋਧ ਜੋਧੰ। ਤਜੈ ਬਾਣ ਕ੍ਰੋਧੰ।","roman":"Jute jodh jodhan | tajai baan krodhan |","meaning_en":"Warrior closed with warrior, loosing arrows in wrath;","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਟੈ ਅੰਗ ਭੰਗੰ। ਭ੍ਰਮੇ ਰੰਗ ਜੰਗੰ। ੫੩੬।","roman":"Tutai ang bhangan | bhrame rang jangan | 536 |","meaning_en":"limbs break and are severed; (warriors) wander in the colour of war.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[537],"number_text":"੫੩੭।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੇ ਈਸ ਭੀਸੰ। ਪੁਐ ਮਾਲ ਸੀਸੰ।","roman":"Nache ees bheesan | puai maal seesan |","meaning_en":"The terrible Shiva dances, stringing a garland of heads;","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੈ ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਚਾਰੰ। ਤਜੈ ਬਾਣ ਧਾਰੰ। ੫੩੭।","roman":"Karai chitr chaaran | tajai baan dhaaran | 537 |","meaning_en":"(the warrior) makes fine wondrous (moves), loosing streams of arrows.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[538],"number_text":"੫੩੮।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੰਡੇ ਜੋਧ ਜੋਧੰ। ਤਜੇ ਬਾਣ ਕ੍ਰੋਧੰ।","roman":"Mande jodh jodhan | taje baan krodhan |","meaning_en":"Warrior engaged warrior, loosing arrows in wrath;","page":774,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਦੀ ਸ੍ਰੋਣ ਪੂਰੰ। ਫਿਰੀ ਗੈਣ ਹੂਰੰ। ੫੩੮।","roman":"Nadee sron pooran | phiree gain hooran | 538 |","meaning_en":"rivers ran full of blood; houris roamed the sky.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[539],"number_text":"੫੩੯।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਸੈ ਮੁੰਡ ਮਾਲਾ। ਤਜੈ ਜੋਗ ਜ੍ਵਾਲਾ।","roman":"Hasai mund maalaa | tajai jog jvaalaa |","meaning_en":"The one with the garland of heads laughs, and casts out the flame of yoga;","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Understood as Shiva (or Kali); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜੈ ਬਾਣ ਜ੍ਵਾਣੰ। ਗ੍ਰਸੈ ਦੁਸਟ ਪ੍ਰਾਣੰ। ੫੩੯।","roman":"Tajai baan jvaanan | grasai dusat praanan | 539 |","meaning_en":"young warriors loose arrows that seize the lives of the wicked.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[540],"number_text":"੫੪੦।","page":774,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੇ ਘੁੰਮਿ ਭੂਮੀ। ਉਠੀ ਧੂਰ ਧੂੰਮੀ।","roman":"Gire ghunmi bhoomee | uthee dhoor dhoonmee |","meaning_en":"They fall, reeling, to the ground; dust rises like smoke.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਭੇ ਰੇਤ ਖੇਤੰ। ਨਚੇ ਭੂਤ ਪ੍ਰੇਤੰ। ੫੪੦।","roman":"Subhe ret khetan | nache bhoot pretan | 540 |","meaning_en":"The sand of the field looks splendid; ghosts and spirits dance.","page":774,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[541],"number_text":"੫੪੧।","page":775,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਿਲਿਓ ਚੀਨ ਰਾਜਾ। ਭਏ ਸਰਬ ਕਾਜਾ।","roman":"Milio cheen raajaa | bhae sarab kaajaa |","meaning_en":"The king of China came and submitted; all the tasks were accomplished.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਇਓ ਸੰਗ ਕੈ ਕੈ। ਚਲਿਓ ਅਗ੍ਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ। ੫੪੧।","roman":"Laio sang kai kai | chalio agr hvai kai | 541 |","meaning_en":"He took him along, and went on ahead.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਛਪੈ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਛਪੈ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Chhapai chhand","meaning_en":"Chhapai metre.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[542],"number_text":"੫੪੨।","page":775,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਏ ਸੰਗ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਸਰਬ ਬਜੇ ਬਿਜਈ ਦੁੰਦਭਿ ਰਣ।","roman":"Lae sang nrip sarab baje bijaee dundbhi ran |","meaning_en":"He took all the kings with him; the drums of victory sounded on the field.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਭੇ ਸੂਰ ਸੰਗ੍ਰਾਮ ਨਿਰਖਿ ਰੀਝਈ ਅਪਛਰ ਗਣ।","roman":"Subhe soor sangraam nirkhi reejhaee apchhar gan |","meaning_en":"The heroes look splendid in the battle; seeing them, the hosts of apsaras are pleased.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਕੇ ਦੇਵ ਆਦੇਵ ਜਕੇ ਗੰਧਰਬ ਜਛ ਬਰ।","roman":"Chhake dev aadev jake gandhrab jachh bar |","meaning_en":"Gods and demons were amazed, the Gandharvas and noble Yakshas astonished;","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਕੇ ਭੂਤ ਅਰੁ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਸਰਬ ਬਿਦਿਆਧਰ ਨਰ ਬਰ।","roman":"Chake bhoot aru pret sarab bidiaadhar nar bar |","meaning_en":"ghosts and spirits, all the Vidyadhars and the best of men were astonished.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖੰਕੜੀਯ ਕਾਲ ਕ੍ਰ�ਰਾ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਬਹੁ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਰ ਉਸਤਤਿ ਕਰੀਯ।","roman":"Khankreey kaal kra(?)raa prabhaa bahu prakaar usatti kareey |","meaning_en":"Kal, fierce and radiant, laughed harshly and praised him in many ways;","page":775,"flags":[{"code":"0xad","reason":"unresolved: draws an empty box in the PDF itself: the source font lacks this glyph"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖੰਕੜੀਯ: read as 'laughed harshly'; uncertain. Printed with a broken character in ਕ੍ਰ�ਰਾ; read as ਕ੍ਰੂਰਾ 'fierce'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਖੰਡਨ ਅਖੰਡ ਚੰਡੀ ਮਹਾ ਜਯ ਜਯ ਜਯ ਸਬਦੋਚਰੀਯ। ੫੪੨।","roman":"Khandan akhand chandee mahaa jay jay jay sabdochreey | 542 |","meaning_en":"great Chandi, breaker of the unbreakable, uttered the cry 'Victory, victory, victory!'","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[543],"number_text":"੫੪੩।","page":775,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਿੜਿਯ ਭੇੜ ਲੜਖੜਿਯ ਮੇਰੁ ਝੜਪੜਿਯ ਪਤ੍ਰ ਬਣ।","roman":"Bhiriy bher larakhriy meru jharapriy patr ban |","meaning_en":"The armies clashed, Mount Meru tottered, the leaves of the forests fell;","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡੁਲਿਯ ਇੰਦੁ ਤੜਫੜ ਫਨਿੰਦ ਸੰਕੁੜਿਯ ਦ੍ਰਵਣ ਗਣ।","roman":"Duliy indu tarphar phanind sankuriy dravan gan |","meaning_en":"the moon wavered, the king of serpents writhed, the hosts of demons shrank;","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦ੍ਰਵਣ: read as 'demons' (danavs); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਕਿਯੋ ਗਇੰਦ ਧਧਕਯ ਚੰਦ ਭੰਭਜਗ ਦਿਵਾਕਰ।","roman":"Chakiyo gaind dhadhkay chand bhanbhjag divaakar |","meaning_en":"the great elephant (of the quarters) was startled, the moon blazed, the sun fled;","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਇੰਦ: 'elephant' (perhaps Airavat); ਧਧਕਯ ਚੰਦ: 'the moon flared/was alarmed'. Uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਡੁਲਗ ਸੁਮੇਰੁ ਡਗਗ ਕੁਮੇਰ ਸਭ ਸੁਕਗ ਸਾਇਰ।","roman":"Dulag sumeru dagag kumer sabh sukag saair |","meaning_en":"Sumeru shook, Kuber staggered, and all the oceans dried up.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਤਜਗ ਧ੍ਯਾਨ ਤਬ ਧੂਰਜਟੀ ਸਹਿ ਨ ਭਾਰ ਸਕਗ ਥਿਰਾ।","roman":"Tatjag dhyaan tab dhoorajtee sahi na bhaar sakag thiraa |","meaning_en":"Then Dhurjati (Shiva) abandoned his meditation; the earth could not bear the weight.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਛਲਗ ਨੀਰ ਪਛੁਲਗ ਪਵਨ ਸੁ ਡਗ ਡਗ ਡਗ ਕੰਪਗੁ ਧਰਾ। ੫੪੩।","roman":"Uchhlag neer pachhulag pavan su dag dag dag kanpgu dharaa | 543 |","meaning_en":"The waters leapt up, the wind turned back, and the earth trembled and shook.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਡਗ ਡਗ ਡਗ: sound-word for shaking."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[544],"number_text":"੫੪੪।","page":775,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲਗੁ ਬਾਣੁ ਰੁਕਿਗ ਦਿਸਾਣ ਪਬ੍ਯ ਪਿਸਾਨ ਹੂਅ।","roman":"Chalgu baanu rukig disaan paby pisaan hooa |","meaning_en":"The arrows flew and blocked the directions; the mountains were ground to flour.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਬ੍ਯ ਪਿਸਾਨ ਹੂਅ: 'mountains became flour'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਿਗਗੁ ਬਿੰਧ ਉਛਲਗੁ ਸਿੰਧੁ ਕੰਪਗੁ ਸੁਨਿ ਮੁਨਿ ਧੂਅ।","roman":"Diggu bindh uchhalgu sindhu kanpgu suni muni dhooa |","meaning_en":"Vindhya fell, the ocean surged, and hearing it, the sage Dhru trembled.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧੂਅ: read as Dhru (the pole star); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਹਮ ਬੇਦ ਤਜ ਭਜਗੁ ਇੰਦ੍ਰ ਇੰਦ੍ਰਾਸਣਿ ਤਜਗੁ।","roman":"Braham bed taj bhajgu indr indraasni tajgu |","meaning_en":"Brahma abandoned the Vedas and fled; Indra left Indra's throne,","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਦਿਨ ਕ੍ਰੂਰ ਕਲਕੀਵਤਾਰ ਕ੍ਰੁਧਤ ਰਣਿ ਗਜਗੁ।","roman":"Jadin kroor kalkeevtaar krudhat rani gajgu |","meaning_en":"on the day the fierce Kalki incarnation roared in wrath on the battlefield.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਛਰੰਤ ਧੂਰਿ ਬਾਜਨ ਖੁਰੀਯ ਸਬ ਅਕਾਸ ਮਗੁ ਛਾਇ ਲੀਅ।","roman":"Uchhrant dhoori baajan khureey sab akaas magu chhaai leea |","meaning_en":"The dust thrown up by the horses' hooves covered the whole path of the sky,","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਣੁ ਰਚੀਯ ਲੋਕ ਕਰਿ ਕੋਪ ਹਰਿ ਅਸਟਕਾਸ ਖਟੁ ਧਰਣਿ ਕੀਅ। ੫੪੪।","roman":"Janu racheey lok kari kop hari asatkaas khatu dharni keea | 544 |","meaning_en":"as if the Lord, in wrath, had made the worlds anew, making eight skies and six earths.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Reading: the dust rose so that the seven heavens became eight and the seven earths six; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[545],"number_text":"੫੪੫।","page":775,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਚਾਰੁ ਚਕ੍ਰਵੇ ਚਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਸਿਰ ਸਹੰਸ ਸੇਸ ਫਣ।","roman":"Chakrit chaaru chakrave chakrit sir sahans ses phan |","meaning_en":"The fair circle of the world was startled, and so were the thousand hooded heads of Shesh;","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਕ੍ਰਵੇ: read as 'the circle (of the earth)' or 'the chakravaka birds'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਕਤ ਮਛ ਮਾਵਾਸ ਛੋਡਿ ਰਣ ਭਜਗ ਦ੍ਰਵਣ ਗਣ।","roman":"Dhakat machh maavaas chhodi ran bhajag dravan gan |","meaning_en":"the fish quaked; leaving their strongholds and the field, the hosts of demons fled.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧਕਤ ਮਛ: perhaps the fish that bears the earth; ਦ੍ਰਵਣ: read as 'demons'. Uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭ੍ਰਮਤ ਕਾਕ ਕੁੰਡਲੀਅ ਗਿਧ ਉਧਹੂੰ ਲੇ ਉਡੀਯ।","roman":"Bhramat kaak kundleea gidh udhhoon le udeey |","meaning_en":"Crows wheel about, and vultures carry off (flesh) up into the sky;","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੁੰਡਲੀਅ: 'in circles'; ਉਧਹੂੰ: 'upward'. Uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਮਤ ਜ੍ਵਾਲ ਖੰਕਾਲਿ ਲੁਥ ਹਥੋਂ ਨਹੀ ਛੁਟੀਯ।","roman":"Bamat jvaal khankaali luth hathon nahee chhuteey |","meaning_en":"Kali spits flames, and the corpse does not leave her hands.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖੰਕਾਲਿ: read as 'Kali' (or a skeleton-like goddess); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਟੁਟੰਤ ਟੋਪ ਫੁਟੰਤ ਜਿਰਹ ਦਸਤਰਾਗ ਪਖਰ ਤੁਰੀਯ।","roman":"Tutant top phutant jirah dasatraag pakhar tureey |","meaning_en":"Helmets break, chain-mail splits, (as do) the gauntlets and the armour of the horses.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਸਤਰਾਗ: read as 'gauntlets'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਜੰਤ ਭੀਰ ਰਿਝੰਤ ਮਨ ਨਿਰਖਿ ਸੂਰ ਹੂਰੇ ਫਿਰੀਯ। ੫੪੫।","roman":"Bhajant bheer rijhant man nirkhi soor hoore phireey | 545 |","meaning_en":"The cowards flee; the houris roam about, pleased at heart, watching the heroes.","page":775,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਮਾਧੋ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਮਾਧੋ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Maadho chhand","meaning_en":"Madho metre.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[546],"number_text":"੫੪੬।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਕੋਪਾ ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰਾ। ਬਾਜਤ ਤੂਰ ਹੋਤ ਝਨਕਾਰਾ।","roman":"Jab kopaa kalkee avtaaraa | baajat toor hot jhankaaraa |","meaning_en":"When the Kalki incarnation became angry, trumpets sounded and there was a clashing;","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾ ਹਾ ਮਾਧੋ ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਸੰਭਾਰੇ। ਪੈਠੇ ਸੁਭਟ ਹਥ੍ਯਾਰ ਉਘਾਰੇ। ੫੪੬।","roman":"Haa haa maadho baan kamaan kripaan sanbhaare | paithe subhat hathyaar ughaare | 546 |","meaning_en":"ha ha Madho! They took up arrows, bows and swords; the fine warriors entered (the fight) with weapons drawn.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"'Ha ha Madho' is the metre's refrain, left as is."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[547],"number_text":"੫੪੭।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲੀਨ ਮਚੀਨ ਦੇਸ ਕਾ ਰਾਜਾ। ਤਾ ਦਿਨ ਬਜੇ ਜੁਝਾਊ ਬਾਜਾ।","roman":"Leen macheen des kaa raajaa | taa din baje jujhaaoo baajaa |","meaning_en":"He captured the king of the land of Machin; that day the war-music sounded;","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾ ਹਾ ਮਾਧੋ ਦੇਸ ਦੇਸ ਕੇ ਛਤ੍ਰ ਛਿਨਾਏ। ਦੇਸ ਬਿਦੇਸ ਤੁਰੰਗ ਫਿਰਾਏ। ੫੪੭।","roman":"Haa haa maadho des des ke chhatr chhinaae | des bides turang phiraae | 547 |","meaning_en":"ha ha Madho! He snatched the canopies of land after land, and rode his horses through lands far and near.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[548],"number_text":"੫੪੮।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚੀਨ ਮਚੀਨ ਛੀਨ ਜਬ ਲੀਨਾ। ਉਤਰ ਦੇਸ ਪਯਾਨਾ ਕੀਨਾ।","roman":"Cheen macheen chheen jab leenaa | utar des payaanaa keenaa |","meaning_en":"When he had seized China and Machin, he set out for the northern lands;","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾ ਹਾ ਮਾਧੋ ਕਹ ਲੌ ਗਨੋ ਉਤਰੀ ਰਾਜਾ। ਸਭ ਸਿਰਿ ਡੰਕ ਜੀਤ ਕਾ ਬਾਜਾ। ੫੪੮।","roman":"Haa haa maadho kah lau gano utree raajaa | sabh siri dank jeet kaa baajaa | 548 |","meaning_en":"ha ha Madho! How many northern kings can I count? Over the heads of all, the drum of victory sounded.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[549],"number_text":"੫੪੯।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਬਿਧਿ ਜੀਤਿ ਜੀਤ ਕੈ ਰਾਜਾ। ਸਭ ਸਿਰਿ ਨਾਦ ਬਿਜੈ ਕਾ ਬਾਜਾ।","roman":"Ih bidhi jeeti jeet kai raajaa | sabh siri naad bijai kaa baajaa |","meaning_en":"In this way the king conquered again and again; the call of victory sounded over all;","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾ ਹਾ ਮਾਧੋ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਛਾਡਿ ਦੇਸ ਭਜਿ ਚਲੇ। ਜਿਤ ਤਿਤ ਦੀਹ ਦਨੁਜ ਦਲ ਮਲੇ। ੫੪੯।","roman":"Haa haa maadho jah tah chhaadi des bhaji chale | jit tit deeh danuj dal male | 549 |","meaning_en":"ha ha Madho! Everywhere (people) left their lands and fled; everywhere the huge demon armies were crushed.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[550],"number_text":"੫੫੦।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੀਨੇ ਜਗ ਅਨੇਕ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਰਾ। ਦੇਸਿ ਦੇਸ ਕੇ ਜੀਤਿ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਾਰਾ।","roman":"Keene jag anek prakaaraa | desi des ke jeeti nripaaraa |","meaning_en":"He performed sacrifices of many kinds, having conquered the kings of land after land;","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾ ਹਾ ਮਾਧੋ ਦੇਸ ਬਿਦੇਸ ਭੇਟ ਲੈ ਆਏ। ਸੰਤ ਉਬਾਰਿ ਅਸੰਤ ਖਪਾਏ। ੫੫੦।","roman":"Haa haa maadho des bides bhet lai aae | sant ubaari asant khapaae | 550 |","meaning_en":"ha ha Madho! From lands near and far they came bringing gifts; he saved the saintly and destroyed the wicked.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[551],"number_text":"੫੫੧।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਚਲੀ ਧਰਮ ਕੀ ਬਾਤਾ। ਪਾਪਹਿ ਜਾਤ ਭਈ ਸੁਧਿ ਸਾਤਾ।","roman":"Jah tah chalee dharam kee baataa | paaphi jaat bhaee sudhi saataa |","meaning_en":"Everywhere talk of dharma spread; as sin departed, (people) came to awareness and peace;","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਧਿ ਸਾਤਾ: 'awareness and peace'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾ ਹਾ ਮਾਧੋ ਕਲਿ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਜੀਤ ਘਰ ਆਏ। ਜਹ ਤਹ ਹੋਵਨ ਲਾਗ ਬਧਾਏ। ੫੫੧।","roman":"Haa haa maadho kali avtaar jeet ghar aae | jah tah hovan laag badhaae | 551 |","meaning_en":"ha ha Madho! The incarnation of the Kali age came home victorious, and everywhere celebrations began.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[552],"number_text":"੫੫੨।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਲੋ ਕਲਿਜੁਗਾਂਤ ਨੀਯਰਾਯੋ। ਜਹ ਤਹ ਭੇਦ ਸਬਨ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Tab lo kalijugaant neeyraayo | jah tah bhed saban suni paayo |","meaning_en":"By then the end of the Kali age drew near; everywhere all heard the secret;","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾ ਹਾ ਮਾਧੋ ਕਲਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਤਬੈ ਪਹਚਾਨੀ। ਸਤਿਜੁਗ ਕੀ ਆਗਮਤਾ ਜਾਨੀ। ੫੫੨।","roman":"Haa haa maadho kalkee baat tabai pahchaanee | satijug kee aagamtaa jaanee | 552 |","meaning_en":"ha ha Madho! Kalki then recognised the matter, and knew the coming of the Sat age.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅਨਹਦ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਅਨਹਦ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Anhad chhand","meaning_en":"Anahad metre.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[553],"number_text":"੫੫੩।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤਿਜੁਗ ਆਯੋ। ਸਭ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Satijug aayo | sabh suni paayo |","meaning_en":"The Sat age came; all heard of it.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਨਿ ਮਨ ਭਾਯੋ। ਗੁਨ ਗਨ ਗਾਯੋ। ੫੫੩।","roman":"Muni man bhaayo | gun gan gaayo | 553 |","meaning_en":"It pleased the minds of the sages; they sang his many virtues.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[554],"number_text":"੫੫੪।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬ ਜਗ ਜਾਨੀ। ਅਕਥ ਕਹਾਨੀ।","roman":"Sab jag jaanee | akath kahaanee |","meaning_en":"The whole world knew the indescribable story;","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਨਿ ਗਨਿ ਮਾਨੀ। ਕਿਨਹੁ ਨ ਜਾਨੀ। ੫੫੪।","roman":"Muni gani maanee | kinhu na jaanee | 554 |","meaning_en":"the hosts of sages accepted it, (yet) no one truly understood it.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[555],"number_text":"੫੫੫।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭ ਜਗ ਦੇਖਾ। ਅਨ ਅਨ ਭੇਖਾ।","roman":"Sabh jag dekhaa | an an bhekhaa |","meaning_en":"All the world saw (him) in guise after guise,","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਛਬਿ ਬਿਸੇਖਾ। ਸਹਿਤ ਭਿਖੇਖਾ। ੫੫੫।","roman":"Suchhbi bisekhaa | sahit bhikhekhaa | 555 |","meaning_en":"with especially fine beauty, together with the garb of a mendicant.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਿਖੇਖਾ: read as 'mendicant's garb'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[556],"number_text":"੫੫੬।","page":776,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਨਿ ਮਨ ਮੋਹੇ। ਫੁਲ ਗੁਲ ਸੋਹੇ।","roman":"Muni man mohe | phul gul sohe |","meaning_en":"The sages' minds were charmed; flowers and roses looked splendid.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਮ ਛਬਿ ਕੋ ਹੈ। ਐਸੇ ਬਨਿਓ ਹੈ। ੫੫੬।","roman":"Sam chhabi ko hai | aise banio hai | 556 |","meaning_en":"Who is equal to this beauty? Such was the splendour.","page":776,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਤਿਲੋਕੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤਿਲੋਕੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Tilokee chhand","meaning_en":"Tiloki metre.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[557],"number_text":"੫੫੭।","page":777,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤਿਜੁਗ ਆਦਿ ਕਲਿਜੁਗ ਅੰਤਹ। ਜਹ ਤਹ ਆਨੰਦ ਸੰਤ ਮਹੰਤਹ।","roman":"Satijug aadi kalijug antah | jah tah aanand sant mahantah |","meaning_en":"The Sat age began and the Kali age ended; everywhere saints and holy men were in bliss.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਗਾਵਤ ਬਜਾਵਤ ਤਾਲੀ। ਨਾਚਤ ਸਿਵਜੀ ਹਸਤ ਜ੍ਵਾਲੀ। ੫੫੭।","roman":"Jah tah gaavat bajaavat taalee | naachat sivjee hasat jvaalee | 557 |","meaning_en":"Everywhere they sang and clapped; Shiva danced and the Flame (the goddess) laughed.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜ੍ਵਾਲੀ: read as the goddess (Jwala); uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[558],"number_text":"੫੫੮।","page":777,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਜਤ ਡਉਰੂ ਰਾਜਤ ਤੰਤ੍ਰੀ। ਰੀਝਤ ਰਾਜੰ ਸੀਝਸ ਅਤ੍ਰੀ।","roman":"Baajat dauroo raajat tantree | reejhat raajan seejhas atree |","meaning_en":"The damru sounds, the stringed instruments look fine; kings are pleased and warriors (? ਅਤ੍ਰੀ) are fulfilled.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੀਝਸ ਅਤ੍ਰੀ: very uncertain; perhaps 'Atri (the sage) is satisfied' or 'the armed ones are fulfilled'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਜਤ ਤੂਰੰ ਗਾਵਤ ਗੀਤਾ। ਜਹ ਤਹ ਕਲਕੀ ਜੁਧਨ ਜੀਤਾ। ੫੫੮।","roman":"Baajat tooran gaavat geetaa | jah tah kalkee judhan jeetaa | 558 |","meaning_en":"Trumpets sound and songs are sung: everywhere Kalki has won the wars.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਮੋਹਨ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਮੋਹਨ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Mohan chhand","meaning_en":"Mohan metre.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[559],"number_text":"੫੫੯।","page":777,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਿ ਮਾਰਿ ਕੈ ਰਿਪੁ ਟਾਰ ਕੈ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਮੰਡਲੀ ਸੰਗ ਕੈ ਲੀਓ।","roman":"Ari maari kai ripu taar kai nrip mandlee sang kai leeo |","meaning_en":"Killing his foes and driving off his enemies, he took the circle of kings along with him;","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਤ੍ਰ ਤਤ੍ਰ ਜਿਤੇ ਤਿਤੇ ਅਤਿ ਦਾਨ ਮਾਨ ਸਬੈ ਦੀਓ।","roman":"Jatr tatr jite tite ati daan maan sabai deeo |","meaning_en":"wherever they were, he gave them all great gifts and honour.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਰ ਰਾਜ ਜ੍ਯੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਰਾਜ ਹੁਐ ਗਿਰ ਰਾਜ ਸੇ ਭਟ ਮਾਰ ਕੈ।","roman":"Sur raaj jyo nrip raaj huai gir raaj se bhat maar kai |","meaning_en":"Like Indra, king of the gods, he became king of kings, having slain warriors like kings of mountains;","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਖ ਪਾਇ ਹਰਖ ਬਢਾਇਕੈ ਗ੍ਰਹਿ ਆਇਯੋ ਜਸੁ ਸੰਗ ਲੈ। ੫੫੯।","roman":"Sukh paai harakh badhaaikai grahi aaiyo jasu sang lai | 559 |","meaning_en":"finding happiness and increasing joy, he came home bringing glory with him.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[560],"number_text":"੫੬੦।","page":777,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਿ ਜੀਤ ਜੀਤ ਅਭੀਤ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਜਗਿ ਹੋਮ ਜਗ ਘਨੇ ਕਰੇ।","roman":"Ari jeet jeet abheet hvai jagi hom jag ghane kare |","meaning_en":"Conquering foe after foe, fearless, he performed many yagyas and homs;","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਸਿ ਦੇਸਿ ਅਸੇਸ ਭਿਛਕ ਰੋਗ ਸੋਗ ਸਬੈ ਹਰੇ।","roman":"Desi desi ases bhichhak rog sog sabai hare |","meaning_en":"in land after land he removed all the illness and sorrow of countless beggars.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਰ ਰਾਜ ਜਿਉ ਦਿਜ ਰਾਜ ਕੇ ਬਹੁ ਭਾਤਿ ਦਾਰਿਦ ਮਾਰ ਕੈ।","roman":"Kur raaj jiu dij raaj ke bahu bhaati daarid maar kai |","meaning_en":"Like Kuru the king, he did away with the poverty of the Brahmins in many ways;","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੁਰ ਰਾਜ ਜਿਉ ਦਿਜ ਰਾਜ ਕੇ: read as 'like king Kuru, (removing the poverty) of the best Brahmins'; ਦਿਜ ਰਾਜ could also mean the moon. Uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗੁ ਜੀਤਿ ਸੰਭਰ ਕੋ ਚਲਯੋ ਜਗਿ ਜਿਤ ਕਿਤ ਬਿਥਾਰ ਕੈ। ੫੬੦।","roman":"Jagu jeeti sanbhar ko chalyo jagi jit kit bithaar kai | 560 |","meaning_en":"having conquered the world, he went to Sambhal, spreading sacrifices everywhere.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੰਭਰ: read as Sambhal (Kalki's city)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[561],"number_text":"੫੬੧।","page":777,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗ ਜੀਤਿ ਬੇਦ ਬਿਥਾਰ ਕੇ ਜਗ ਸੁ ਅਰਥ ਅਰਥ ਚਿਤਾਰੀਅੰ।","roman":"Jag jeeti bed bithaar ke jag su arath arath chitaareean |","meaning_en":"Having conquered the world and spread the Vedas, he called to mind sacrifices for every purpose;","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਗ ਸੁ ਅਰਥ ਅਰਥ ਚਿਤਾਰੀਅੰ: 'thought of yagyas for each aim'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਸਿ ਦੇਸਿ ਬਿਦੇਸ ਮੈ ਨਵ ਭੇਜਿ ਭੇਜਿ ਹਕਾਰੀਅੰ।","roman":"Desi desi bides mai nav bheji bheji hakaareean |","meaning_en":"in land after land, at home and abroad, he sent out again and again and called (people) in.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਵ: 'anew' or 'nine (regions)'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰ ਦਾੜ ਜਿਉ ਰਣ ਗਾੜ ਹੁਇ ਤਿਰਲੋਕ ਜੀਤ ਸਬੈ ਲੀਏ।","roman":"Dhar daar jiu ran gaar hui tirlok jeet sabai lee'e |","meaning_en":"Like the Boar (lifting the earth) on his tusk, firm in battle, he conquered all three worlds and took them.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧਰ ਦਾੜ: read as 'earth-on-tusk', i.e. the Boar incarnation; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁ ਦਾਨ ਦੈ ਸਨਮਾਨ ਸੇਵਕ ਭੇਜ ਭੇਜ ਤਹਾ ਦੀਏ। ੫੬੧।","roman":"Bahu daan dai sanmaan sevak bhej bhej tahaa dee'e | 561 |","meaning_en":"Giving many gifts and honours, he sent his servants out (to rule) there.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[562],"number_text":"੫੬੨।","page":777,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖਲ ਖੰਡਿ ਖੰਡਿ ਬਿਹੰਡ ਕੈ ਅਰਿ ਦੰਡ ਦੰਡ ਬਡੋ ਦੀਯੋ।","roman":"Khal khandi khandi bihand kai ari dand dand bado deeyo |","meaning_en":"Cutting the wicked to pieces and destroying them, he dealt the enemy heavy punishment;","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਬ ਖਰਬ ਅਦਰਬ ਦਿਰਬ ਸੁ ਜੀਤ ਕੈ ਆਪਨੋ ਕੀਯੋ।","roman":"Arab kharab adrab dirab su jeet kai aapno keeyo |","meaning_en":"wealth by the billions and trillions, and things beyond wealth, he won and made his own.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਦਰਬ ਦਿਰਬ: 'wealth and what is not wealth'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਜੀਤ ਜੀਤ ਅਜੀਤ ਜੋਧਨ ਛਤ੍ਰ ਅਤ੍ਰ ਛਿਨਾਈਅੰ।","roman":"Ranjeet jeet ajeet jodhan chhatr atr chhinaaeean |","meaning_en":"Victorious in battle, he conquered the unconquered warriors and took away their canopies and weapons.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰਦਾਰ ਬਿੰਸਤਿ ਚਾਰ ਕਲਿ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਛਤ੍ਰ ਫਿਰਾਈਅੰ। ੫੬੨।","roman":"Sardaar binsti chaar kali avtaar chhatr phiraaeean | 562 |","meaning_en":"The twenty-fourth chief, the incarnation of the Kali age, had his canopy carried round (over the world).","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਿੰਸਤਿ ਚਾਰ: 'twenty-four', i.e. the twenty-fourth incarnation."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਮਥਾਨ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਮਥਾਨ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Mathaan chhand","meaning_en":"Mathan metre.","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[563],"number_text":"੫੬੩।","page":777,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛਾਜੈ ਮਹਾ ਜੋਤਿ। ਭਾਨੰ ਮਨੋਦੋਤਿ।","roman":"Chhaajai mahaa joti | bhaanan manodoti |","meaning_en":"A great light shines, radiant as the sun;","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗਿ ਸੰਕ ਤਜ ਦੀਨ। ਮਿਲਿ ਬੰਦਨਾ ਕੀਨ। ੫੬੩।","roman":"Jagi sank taj deen | mili bandnaa keen | 563 |","meaning_en":"the world gave up its doubt and together bowed (to him).","page":777,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[564],"number_text":"੫੬੪।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਜੈ ਮਹਾ ਰੂਪ। ਲਾਜੈ ਸਬੈ ਭੂਪ।","roman":"Raajai mahaa roop | laajai sabai bhoop |","meaning_en":"His great beauty shines; all the kings are put to shame.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗ ਆਨ ਮਾਨੀਸੁ। ਮਿਲਿ ਭੇਟ ਲੈ ਦੀਸੁ।੫੬੪।","roman":"Jag aan maaneesu | mili bhet lai deesu | 564 |","meaning_en":"The world accepted his command, and they came together and gave him offerings.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਆਨ: 'command/authority'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[565],"number_text":"੫੬੫।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਭੇ ਮਹਾਰਾਜ। ਅਛ੍ਰੀ ਰਹੈ ਲਾਜ।","roman":"Sobhe mahaaraaj | achhree rahai laaj |","meaning_en":"The great king looks splendid; the apsaras are abashed.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਰੀਝਿ ਮਧੁ ਬੈਨ। ਰਸ ਰੰਗ ਭਰੇ ਨੈਨ। ੫੬੫।","roman":"Ati reejhi madhu bain | ras rang bhare nain | 565 |","meaning_en":"Very pleased, (they speak) sweet words, their eyes full of delight and love.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[566],"number_text":"੫੬੬।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਹਤ ਅਨੂਪਾਛ। ਕਾਛੇ ਮਨੋ ਕਾਛ।","roman":"Sohat anoopaachh | kaachhe mano kaachh |","meaning_en":"His incomparable eyes look fine, as if (an actor) had put on a costume;","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਨੂਪਾਛ: read as 'incomparable eyes' (anupa-akshi); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੀਝੈ ਸੁਰੀ ਦੇਖਿ। ਰਾਵਲੜੇ ਭੇਖਿ। ੫੬੬।","roman":"Reejhai suree dekhi | raavalre bhekhi | 566 |","meaning_en":"seeing him in a Rawal's garb, the goddesses are delighted.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਾਵਲੜੇ: 'of a Rawal (yogi)'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[567],"number_text":"੫੬੭।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖੇ ਜਿਨੈ ਨੈਕੁ। ਲਾਗੈ ਤਿਸੈ ਐਖ।","roman":"Dekhe jinai naiku | laagai tisai aikh |","meaning_en":"Whoever sees him even a little, it strikes them like an arrow (in the eye);","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਐਖ: read as 'arrow' or 'eye'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੀਝੈ ਸੁਰੀ ਨਾਰਿ। ਦੇਖੈ ਧਰੇ ਪ੍ਯਾਰ। ੫੬੭।","roman":"Reejhai suree naari | dekhai dhare pyaar | 567 |","meaning_en":"the women of the gods are delighted and look at him with love.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[568],"number_text":"੫੬੮।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੰਗੇ ਮਹਾ ਰੰਗ। ਲਾਜੈ ਲਖਿ ਅਨੰਗ।","roman":"Range mahaa rang | laajai lakhi anang |","meaning_en":"He is dyed in great love; seeing him, Kamdev is ashamed.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਨੰਗ: Kamdev, god of love."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਿਤਗੰ ਚਿਰੈ ਸਤ੍ਰ। ਲਗੈ ਜਨੋ ਅਤ੍ਰ। ੫੬੮।","roman":"Chitgan chirai satr | lagai jano atr | 568 |","meaning_en":"He pierces the hearts of enemies, as if a weapon struck them.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਿਤਗੰ ਚਿਰੈ ਸਤ੍ਰ: uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[569],"number_text":"੫੬੯।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਭੇ ਮਹਾ ਸੋਭ। ਅਛ੍ਰੀ ਰਹੈ ਲੋਭਿ।","roman":"Sobhe mahaa sobh | achhree rahai lobhi |","meaning_en":"He shines with great splendour; the apsaras are filled with longing.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਂਜੇ ਇਸੇ ਨੈਨ। ਜਾਗੇ ਮਨੋ ਰੈਨ। ੫੬੯।","roman":"Aanje ise nain | jaage mano rain | 569 |","meaning_en":"His eyes are so darkened with kohl, as if he had kept awake all night.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[570],"number_text":"੫੭੦।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੂਪੰ ਭਰੇ ਰਾਗ। ਸੋਭੇ ਸੁ ਸੁਹਾਗ।","roman":"Roopan bhare raag | sobhe su suhaag |","meaning_en":"His form is full of love; he shines with good fortune;","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਹਾਗ: 'marital good fortune'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਛੇ ਨਟੰ ਰਾਜ। ਨਾਚੈ ਮਨੋ ਬਾਜ। ੫੭੦।","roman":"Kaachhe natan raaj | naachai mano baaj | 570 |","meaning_en":"dressed like the king of dancers, he moves as if a horse were dancing.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਜ: read as 'horse' (or 'music', 'falcon'); uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[571],"number_text":"੫੭੧।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਖੈ ਮਨੋ ਬਾਨ। ਕੈਧੋ ਧਰੇ ਸਾਨ।","roman":"Aakhai mano baan | kaidho dhare saan |","meaning_en":"His eyes are like arrows, or as if sharpened on a whetstone;","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਨੇ ਲਗੇ ਜਾਹਿ। ਯਾ ਕੋ ਕਹੈ ਕਾਹਿ। ੫੭੧।","roman":"Jaane lage jaahi | yaa ko kahai kaahi | 571 |","meaning_en":"only the one they strike knows it; who can describe it?","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੁਖਦਾ ਬ੍ਰਿਦ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸੁਖਦਾ ਬ੍ਰਿਦ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Sukhdaa brid chhand","meaning_en":"Sukhda Brid metre.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[572],"number_text":"੫੭੨।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਕਾਛੇ ਕਾਛ ਧਾਰੀ ਹੈਂ। ਕਿ ਰਾਜਾ ਅਧਿਕਾਰੀ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Ki kaachhe kaachh dhaaree hain | ki raajaa adhikaaree hain |","meaning_en":"Is he someone dressed in a costume, or a ruling king?","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਭਾਗ ਕੋ ਸੁਹਾਗ ਹੈਂ। ਕਿ ਰੰਗੋ ਅਨੁਰਾਗ ਹੈਂ। ੫੭੨।","roman":"Ki bhaag ko suhaag hain | ki rango anuraag hain | 572 |","meaning_en":"Is he the good fortune of destiny, or one dyed in love?","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[573],"number_text":"੫੭੩।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਛੋਭੈ ਛਤ੍ਰ ਧਾਰੀ ਛੈ। ਕਿ ਛਤ੍ਰੀ ਅਤ੍ਰ ਵਾਰੀ ਛੈ।","roman":"Ki chhobhai chhatr dhaaree chhai | ki chhatree atr vaaree chhai |","meaning_en":"Is he a stirred canopy-bearer, or a Kshatriya bearing weapons?","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛੋਭੈ: 'stirred' or 'adorned'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਆਂਜੇ ਬਾਨ ਬਾਨੀ ਸੇ। ਕਿ ਕਾਛੀ ਕਾਛ ਕਾਰੀ ਹੈਂ। ੫੭੩।","roman":"Ki aanje baan baanee se | ki kaachhee kaachh kaaree hain | 573 |","meaning_en":"Are (his eyes) darkened like arrows, or is he an actor in costume?","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਆਂਜੇ ਬਾਨ ਬਾਨੀ ਸੇ: uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[574],"number_text":"੫੭੪।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਕਾਮੀ ਕਾਮ ਬਾਨ ਸੇ। ਕਿ ਫੂਲੇ ਫੂਲ ਮਾਲ ਸੇ।","roman":"Ki kaamee kaam baan se | ki phoole phool maal se |","meaning_en":"Is he a lover like the arrow of Kamdev, or blooming like a garland of flowers?","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਰੰਗੇ ਰੰਗ ਰਾਗ ਸੇ। ਕਿ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਸੁਹਾਗ ਸੇ। ੫੭੪।","roman":"Ki range rang raag se | ki sundar suhaag se | 574 |","meaning_en":"Is he dyed in the colour of love, or beautiful like good fortune itself?","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[575],"number_text":"੫੭੫।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਨਾਗਨੀ ਕੇ ਏਸ ਹੈਂ। ਕਿ ਮ੍ਰਿਗੀ ਕੇ ਨਰੇਸ ਛੈ।","roman":"Ki naagnee ke es hain | ki mrigee ke nares chhai |","meaning_en":"Is he lord of the serpent-maidens, or king of the deer?","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਰਾਜਾ ਛਤ੍ਰ ਧਾਰੀ ਹੈਂ। ਕਿ ਕਾਲੀ ਕੇ ਭਿਖਾਰੀ ਛੈ। ੫੭੫।","roman":"Ki raajaa chhatr dhaaree hain | ki kaalee ke bhikhaaree chhai | 575 |","meaning_en":"Is he a canopied king, or a beggar at Kali's door?","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","roman":"Sorthaa","meaning_en":"Sortha.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[576],"number_text":"੫੭੬।","page":778,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਮ ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰਿ ਜੀਤੇ ਜੁਧ ਸਬੈ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਤਿ।","roman":"Im kalkee avtaari jeete judh sabai nripti |","meaning_en":"Thus the Kalki incarnation won the war against all the kings,","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੀਨੋ ਰਾਜ ਸੁਧਾਰਿ ਬੀਸ ਸਹਸ ਦਸ ਲਛ ਬਰਖ। ੫੭੬।","roman":"Keeno raaj sudhaari bees sahas das lachh barakh | 576 |","meaning_en":"and ruled well for ten lakh and twenty thousand years.","page":778,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬੀਸ ਸਹਸ ਦਸ ਲਛ: 'twenty thousand (and) ten lakh'; reading of the number uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਾਵਣਬਾਦ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਵਣਬਾਦ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Raavanbaad chhand","meaning_en":"Ravanbad metre.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[577],"number_text":"੫੭੭।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਹੀ ਸਮਸੇਰ। ਕੀਯੋ ਜੰਗਿ ਜੇਰ। ਦਏ ਮਤਿ ਫੇਰ। ਨ ਲਾਗੀ ਬੇਰ। ੫੭੭।","roman":"Gahee samser | keeyo jangi jer | dae mati pher | na laagee ber | 577 |","meaning_en":"He took up the sword and subdued (them) in war; he turned their minds, and it took no time.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[578],"number_text":"੫੭੮।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦਯੋ ਨਿਜ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ। ਤਜੈ ਸਭ ਤੰਤ੍ਰ। ਲਿਖੈ ਨਿਜ ਜੰਤ੍ਰ। ਸੁ ਬੈਠਿ ਇਕੰਤ੍ਰ। ੫੭੮।","roman":"Dayo nij mantr | tajai sabh tantr | likhai nij jantr | su baithi ikantr | 578 |","meaning_en":"He gave his own mantra, (people) gave up all (other) tantras, and sitting in solitude they wrote his own yantra.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਬਾਨ ਤੁਰੰਗਮ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਤੁਰੰਗਮ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Baan turangam chhand","meaning_en":"Ban Turangam metre.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[579],"number_text":"੫੭੯।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਬਿਧ ਰੂਪ ਸੋਭੈ। ਅਨਿਕ ਲੋਗ ਲੋਭੈ।","roman":"Bibidh roop sobhai | anik log lobhai |","meaning_en":"He shines in various forms; many people are charmed.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਮਿਤ ਤੇਜ ਤਾਹਿ। ਨਿਗਮ ਗਨਤ ਜਾਹਿ। ੫੭੯।","roman":"Amit tej taahi | nigam ganat jaahi | 579 |","meaning_en":"His radiance is boundless; the scriptures go on counting it.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[580],"number_text":"੫੮੦।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਨਿਕ ਭੇਖ ਤਾ ਕੇ। ਬਿਬਿਧ ਰੂਪ ਵਾ ਕੇ।","roman":"Anik bhekh taa ke | bibidh roop vaa ke |","meaning_en":"He has many guises and various forms;","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਨੂਪ ਰੂਪ ਰਾਜੈ। ਬਿਲੋਕਿ ਪਾਪ ਭਾਜੈ। ੫੮੦।","roman":"Anoop roop raajai | biloki paap bhaajai | 580 |","meaning_en":"his incomparable form shines; seeing it, sin flees.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[581],"number_text":"੫੮੧।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਸੇਖ ਪ੍ਰਬਲ ਜੇ ਹੁਤੇ। ਅਨੂਪ ਰੂਪ ਸੰਜੁਤੇ।","roman":"Bisekh prabal je hute | anoop roop sanjute |","meaning_en":"Those who were especially mighty, possessed of incomparable beauty,","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਮਿਤ ਅਰਿ ਘਾਵਹੀਂ। ਜਗਤ ਜਸੁ ਪਾਵਹੀਂ। ੫੮੧।","roman":"Amit ari ghaavheen | jagat jasu paavheen | 581 |","meaning_en":"slay countless enemies and gain glory in the world.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[582],"number_text":"੫੮੨।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਖੰਡ ਬਾਹੁ ਹੈ ਬਲੀ। ਸੁਭੰਤ ਜੋਤਿ ਨਿਰਮਲੀ।","roman":"Akhand baahu hai balee | subhant joti niramlee |","meaning_en":"Unbroken of arm and mighty, they shine with a pure light;","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਹੋਮ ਜਗ ਕੋ ਕਰੈਂ। ਪਰਮ ਪਾਪ ਕੋ ਹਰੈਂ। ੫੮੨।","roman":"Su hom jag ko karain | param paap ko harain | 582 |","meaning_en":"they perform hom and yagya, and take away the greatest sins.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਤੋਮਰ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤੋਮਰ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Tomar chhand","meaning_en":"Tomar metre.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[583],"number_text":"੫੮੩।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗ ਜੀਤਿਓ ਜਬ ਸਰਬ। ਤਬ ਬਾਢਿਓ ਅਤਿ ਗਰਬ।","roman":"Jag jeetio jab sarab | tab baadhio ati garab |","meaning_en":"When he had conquered the whole world, his pride swelled greatly.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੀਅ ਕਾਲ ਪੁਰਖ ਬਿਸਾਰ। ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਕੀਨ ਬਿਚਾਰ। ੫੮੩।","roman":"Deea kaal purakh bisaar | ih bhaati keen bichaar | 583 |","meaning_en":"He forgot Kal Purakh (the Timeless Being), and thought in this way:","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[584],"number_text":"੫੮੪।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਨੁ ਮੋਹਿ ਦੂਸਰ ਨ ਔਰ। ਅਸਿ ਮਾਨ੍ਯੋ ਸਬ ਠਉਰ।","roman":"Binu mohi doosar na aur | asi maanyo sab thaur |","meaning_en":"'Apart from me there is no other.' So he held in every place.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗੁ ਜੀਤਿ ਕੀਨ ਗੁਲਾਮ। ਆਪਨ ਜਪਾਯੋ ਨਾਮ। ੫੮੪।","roman":"Jagu jeeti keen gulaam | aapan japaayo naam | 584 |","meaning_en":"Having conquered the world he made it his slave, and had his own name worshipped.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[585],"number_text":"੫੮੫।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗਿ ਐਸ ਰੀਤਿ ਚਲਾਇ। ਸਿਰ ਅਤ੍ਰ ਪਤ੍ਰ ਫਿਰਾਇ।","roman":"Jagi ais reeti chalaai | sir atr patr phiraai |","meaning_en":"He set such a custom going in the world, carrying the canopy (of rule) over his head;","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬ ਲੋਗ ਆਪਨ ਮਾਨ। ਤਰਿ ਆਂਖਿ ਅਉਰ ਨ ਆਨਿ। ੫੮੫।","roman":"Sab log aapan maan | tari aankhi aur na aani | 585 |","meaning_en":"all people were to regard him alone, and bring no other before their eyes.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਰਿ ਆਂਖਿ ਅਉਰ ਨ ਆਨਿ: 'bring no other into view'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[586],"number_text":"੫੮੬।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਕਾਲ ਪੁਰੁਖ ਜਪੰਤ। ਨਹਿ ਦੇਵਿ ਜਾਪੁ ਭਣੰਤ।","roman":"Nahee kaal purukh japant | nahi devi jaapu bhanant |","meaning_en":"They did not meditate on Kal Purakh, nor recite the name of any god.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਕਾਲ ਦੇਵ ਰਿਸਾਇ। ਇਕ ਅਉਰ ਪੁਰੁਖ ਬਨਾਇ। ੫੮੬।","roman":"Tab kaal dev risaai | ik aur purukh banaai | 586 |","meaning_en":"Then Kal Dev grew angry and made another being.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[587],"number_text":"੫੮੭।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਚਿਅਸੁ ਮਹਿਦੀ ਮੀਰ। ਰਿਸਵੰਤ ਹਾਠ ਹਮੀਰ।","roman":"Rachiasu mahidee meer | risvant haath hameer |","meaning_en":"He created Mahdi Mir, angry, stubborn and mighty.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਾਠ ਹਮੀਰ: 'stubborn chief/hero'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹ ਤਉਨ ਕੋ ਬਧੁ ਕੀਨ। ਪੁਨਿ ਆਪ ਮੋ ਕੀਅ ਲੀਨ। ੫੮੭।","roman":"Tih taun ko badhu keen | puni aap mo keea leen | 587 |","meaning_en":"He slew that one (Kalki), and then (Kal) took him into himself.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Understood: Mahdi Mir slew Kalki, who then merged in Kal; ਆਪ ਮੋ ਕੀਅ ਲੀਨ could refer to either. Uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[588],"number_text":"੫੮੮।","page":779,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗ ਜੀਤਿ ਆਪਨ ਕੀਨ। ਸਬ ਅੰਤਿ ਕਾਲ ਅਧੀਨ।","roman":"Jag jeeti aapan keen | sab anti kaal adheen |","meaning_en":"He conquered the world and made it his own; all in the end are subject to Kal.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਪੂਰਨ ਸੁ ਧਾਰਿ। ਭਏ ਚੌਬਿਸੇ ਅਵਤਾਰ। ੫੮੮।","roman":"Ih bhaati pooran su dhaari | bhae chaubise avtaar | 588 |","meaning_en":"Thus, completed in full, the twenty-four incarnations came to be.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}]}],"ending":{"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਟਕ ਗ੍ਰੰਥੇ ਚਤੁਰ ਬਿਸਤਿ ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਬਰਨਨੰ ਸਮਾਪਤੰ।","roman":"Iti sree bachitr naatak granthe chatur bisti kalkee avtaar barannan samaaptan |","meaning_en":"Here ends, in the book Bachittar Natak, the description of the twenty-fourth, the Kalki incarnation.","page":779,"meaning_status":"draft"}],"page":779}});
